s chip is half lit when a profile has some of the skills), and the profiles chip takes part in the row's fan like any other (`[data-members]` in library.css), so the hand stays in line (Yanzhongixuy on X, 0.1.3926; `library-profile-group.test.cjs`). The page shows a gone agent's chip only on the rows of what it has, lit, so a click takes it out (`withGone` in plugins/library/client.js), leaves it out of All, the per-agent How sheet and every picker, and lists it in By agent as Not installed here with Turn all on off (@jiahao_jayden on X: an uninstalled WorkBuddy was on every skill's row; `TestGoneAgentListedToTakeOut`, `library-gone-agents.test.cjs`). On a Mac WorkBuddy and WorkBuddy AI are detected by their apps' bundle ids (`com.tencent.workbuddy.mac`, `com.workbuddy.workbuddy-ai`, `macBundle`), not by `~/.workbuddy`, which an uninstall leaves and magpie itself writes into (`TestWorkBuddyOnMacIsItsApp`); off a Mac the folder still counts. `everyTarget` keeps it for the guards that refuse an agent's own places: a project folder whose skills folder or MCP file is the agent's, and an instruction set kept in its instructions file. An agent in a running WSL distro has its places under the distro's home (`wslTargetOf`): Claude Code, Codex, Pi, OmO, Gemini CLI, Antigravity CLI, Crush, Cline, CodeBuddy Code, Kimi Code and Goose each by its own rule, never reading this machine's variables (Kimi Code's and Goose's shared `~/.agents/skills` there isn't given), Pi's MCP file chosen by `piMCP` as on this machine from the version the distro's `pi --version` gave its probe (`InstalledVersion`) and the distro's npm folders (`wslPiRoots`; leokon on Discord: only the Windows Pi was offered MCP servers, `TestWSLPiMCP`, `TestWSLMCPSiblings`), and every agent that keeps all of them in its own folder (Hermes Agent, omp, OpenCode, Droid and the rest of `ownFolder`, #1323) by the same rule as on this machine, its MCP file marked as WSL's so a Windows program isn't given to it. A place below a folder the distro has as a link is opened where the link leads (`wslOpen`, agent-wiring's WSL folders that are links, #4502); a link the distro couldn't resolve gives that agent one `wsl` problem and nothing is written to it (`TestWSLFolderIsALinkToC`, `TestWSLFolderLinkUnresolved`). An agent a plugin adds (`a.Plugin`) has the places its plugin's `agent.library` names (`pluginTarget`): an instructions file, an MCP file in one of `agentplug.MCPFormats` (each the `mcpFormat` of the agent it is named for, `pluginMCP`) and a skills folder, `~` and `$VAR` expanded as its config is; one that names none is no target. Before, a plugin's agent got models and keys only. Every built-in agent is a target or is in `noLibrary` with why: OpenBot was added with neither and was in no picker (SSNQT on X), so `TestEveryAgentInLibrary` fails a new agent until it gets one (34 were in no picker when it landed, listed there under #5897). | [`targets.go`](../../internal/library/targets.go) |"
