    "line": "| Stopped WSL distro | A stopped distro's agents are no targets: opening their files would start the distro, or the read fails (#3896). While a distro runs, `keepShape` keeps each agent's places and what its MCP file takes in `wsl.json` (`agent.WSLKeep`, key `library:<kind>`). While it is stopped, `Read` lists its agents from that (`asleepView`, `asleep: <distro>`), ticks as library.json has them; one magpie never saw there is listed only on the rows that name it, as `unseen`, its ticks not shown (cybercaius on Discord: the MCP page knew a distro's agents only once WSL had started). A tick on a stopped agent is kept in library.json as any is (`Takes` accepts one with a known shape; `serversAgents` judges it by `shape.reaches`), nothing is written and nothing in the distro runs; `Woken`, from `KeepLinked`'s loop (and the app's start-up sync), syncs when a distro the library names is seen go from stopped to running (`wsl.exe -l --running`, which starts nothing). The page greys a stopped agent's chip, says so in its tooltip and in one line per distro (`.lib-asleep`); an unseen chip is `aria-disabled` and kept by every click on its row (`keptOf`). The CLI says the same on stderr (`AsleepIn`). Queued, not a start button: a start costs the memory #3896 is about, and All or a bulk tick would start every distro. The Instructions page lists them too (`asleepInstructions`, #4182), at the instructions file the shape keeps, switched on as library.json has them, with what each gets besides (magpie's own folder) and nothing read from the file: its own lines and edits aren't counted then, and its path is plain text, not a reveal, which would open the distro. One switched on whose file magpie never saw is listed as `unseen`, its switch greyed out and kept by every other switch; before, a switch on the page sent the agents without the stopped distro's and took them off. A switch on one is written by `Woken`, which watches a distro named in `Instructions.Agents`, or whos