3	# A bundle is a package that ships this file: the loader applies it as a patch
4	# layer, so the row below is what installing the bundle actually mounts.
5	#
6	# This row is ENABLED by default and carries the full deferral config, so the
7	# whole lifecycle lives in one place:
8	#
9	#   install  ->  plugin_manager install_bundle dsh-tool-gate  (asks first)
10	#   tune     ->  edit the config below and restart
11	#   disable  ->  plugin_manager set_plugin tool-gate-bundle-row false
12	#                (config stays; the tool surface returns to fully expanded)
13	#   remove   ->  plugin_manager remove_bundle dsh-tool-gate
14	#                (the loader drops this whole patch layer — nothing left behind)
15	#
16	# Never hand-copy this row into the profile's own cordis.patch.yml: the bundle
17	# row is already patched in by the loader, and a duplicate mount in the profile
18	# layer would reference a module the manager may remove out from under it —
19	# exactly the dangling-reference failure mode that broke chat startup once.
20	#
21	# On ordering: a patch row can only APPEND to the entry list, so this plugin
22	# cannot be positioned ahead of a provider a bundle declared earlier — and the
